From 9543f9daed861cb378f13488ca43f96f2e3fbace Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:15:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] No allocation on the heap in the usual calls

- the descriptions of the checked views are only concatenated to report
  an error: a successful check of a material data view allocates nothing
  (it allocated about 8 + 6 times the number of material properties and
  external state variables strings at each call).
- the throwing updateValues (and so update and revert of a material data
  manager) report the errors with an error backtrace, which allocates
  nothing unless an error is reported, instead of an execution context.
- AllocationTest: the integration, update and revert of material data
  managers in both layouts and of views, the rotations and the
  evaluations of material properties allocate nothing on the heap in the
  calling thread, for both interfaces.
---
 src/Integrate.cxx            | 100 +++++++++++-------
 src/MaterialStateManager.cxx |  46 +++++++--
 tests/AllocationTest.cxx     | 194 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/CMakeLists.txt         |  15 +++
 4 files changed, 310 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/AllocationTest.cxx

